The E5-int24 candidate arm: the Q4_K x Q8_1 mat-vec computed from the 24-bit
integer multiplier gfx902 runs at full rate, onto
f280b26983ad0fdb705a0d9ebf0503e76f2899b0 after the eight-patch production
series.

RADV reports VK_KHR_shader_integer_dot_product functional and every
integerDotProduct*Accelerated bit false on RAVEN2, and ggml-vulkan.cpp gates
device->integer_dot_product on integerDotProduct4x8BitPackedSignedAccelerated
alone, so the pinned build compiles no _q8_1 mat-vec pipeline and the whole
Q4_K trunk streams through the FP16 dequantize-then-dot family. The same
silicon runs v_mul_u32_u24 and v_mad_u32_u24 at full rate where v_mul_lo_u32
is quarter rate, and ACO selects them for nir_op_imul where
nir_unsigned_upper_bound proves both sources at most 0xffffff
(Mesa 26.2.1 src/amd/compiler/instruction_selection/aco_select_nir_alu.cpp).
This patch computes the packed dot product from masked bytes so every
multiplicand carries that bound.

mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl gains dot_packed_4x8_int24 under GGML_VK_INT24_DOT,
which biases both operands into 0..255 and removes the bias once per call
through sum((au-128)*(bu-128)) = sum(au*bu) - 128*(sum au + sum bu) + 65536,
and a macro puts it behind the extension's own spelling so all forty call
sites read the same. The Q4_K and Q5_K mmvq_dot_product specializes further:
repack4 masks its quant bytes to 0..15, and Q5_K merges one bit above that, so
only the activation byte needs the bias and the correction rides two
accumulators over sixteen values as one shift. Those sixteen products are
written straight-line with literal shifts and literal masks, the way the pinned
function writes four explicit dot calls, so the module holds sixteen multiplies
of constant-masked bytes and indexes the quant vector statically: the compiled
Q4_K variant reaches 46 OpIMul against the extension branch's 30 and the same
73 OpAccessChain. The FP32 tail is byte-identical
to the pinned function, so the replacement is exact against
dotPacked4x8EXT rather than approximate: a C model of both forms agrees with
the signed reference over the whole single-lane domain and four million random
word pairs. mul_mat_vecq.comp requires GL_EXT_integer_dot_product under the
opposite branch of the same define, so the arm compiles on a glslc that
rejects the extension.

GGML_VULKAN_INT24_DOT is a CMake option that reaches both the backend and
vulkan-shaders-gen through the forwarding the extension probes already use,
and both derive GGML_VULKAN_MMVQ_Q8_1_SHADERS from it, so a definition that
lands on one side alone fails at link on arr_dmmv_q4_k_q8_1_f32_data rather
than at device creation. The MMQ and flash-attention int8 shaders have no
replacement and keep reading GGML_VULKAN_INTEGER_DOT_GLSLC_SUPPORT; where they
are absent, ggml_vk_get_mul_mat_mat_pipeline finds an empty pipeline set and
clears quantize_y, so the mat-mat and flash-attention paths stay on the
production shape and the arm changes the mat-vec alone.

GGML_VK_FORCE_INTEGER_DOT=1 admits that mat-vec on a device reporting no
acceleration. It is read once per process, requires an exact "1", and reaches
the device flag and the info line the same way, so one binary runs both arms
and the control is that binary with the variable unset.
